    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293-a1">

                <pb facs="0587" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg491"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 534.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to
                        General Schenck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 8,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note, of the 25th of
                    June last, I have the honor to acquaint you that the secretary of state for the
                    colonies has communicated to me a memorandum received from the governor of
                    Tasmania, stating that instructions will <pb facs="0588" n="492" xml:id="pg492"
                    /> be given for the admission free of duty and wharfage of all instruments,
                    &amp;c., to be used by the expedition from the United States which will visit
                    Hobart Town for the purpose of observing the transit of Venus next year, and
                    that a suitable site for making the observations will be placed at the disposal
                    of the expedition.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
